findings.description:
The change adds destructive behaviour (deleting reminders after repeated failures) and new state transitions with no accompanying tests; there are no `*.test.ts` files under `packages/features/ee/workflows`. At minimum, cover these cases:
- the counter increments when `scheduleSMS` returns a falsy value;
- the counter increments when `scheduleSMS` throws;
- reminders with `retryCount > 1` are deleted, and only SMS ones;
- a failure on one reminder does not stop the rest of the batch.
